"The ER social worker is Priya Raman, thirty-four, quick, practical and hard to shock."
"She comes on at eight and reaches the waiting room by about a quarter past."
"She can place Nala tonight at a women's shelter in Uptown with a bed, meals and a locker."
"Shelter beds open at five in the evening; the day must be spent elsewhere."
"She can give her a transit card loaded with twenty dollars and a bag from the clothing closet."
"An Illinois ID needs a birth certificate or other proof Nala cannot give; it is a long road."
"She refers women leaving a partner to a domestic-violence hotline and to free legal aid."
"She asks few questions about the past and many about tonight: bed, food, warmth, safety."
